+# Pickup reminders
+
+For volunteers considering a different reminder channel or changing pickup reminders. Reminders help members collect
+their pantry orders; they go by SMS because an email trial increased missed pickups and wasted fresh food.
+
+## Delivery
+
+The [reminder implementation](../../larder/reminders.py) sends a reminder of the pickup slot the day before, using
+SMS to the member's phone.
+
+## Why SMS
+
+From April to June 2025, the pantry tried email reminders. The provider reported that 34% of reminder emails were
+never opened. Missed pickups rose from 6% to 13% of pantry orders. A missed pickup leaves a packed bag behind, and
+the fresh food in it goes in the bin at closing time. Many members share a family phone and do not check email;
+they see SMS messages.
+
+The pantry switched back to SMS on July 1, 2025. By August, missed pickups were back to 6%.
+
+Email's lack of sending cost prompted another proposal to replace SMS, which cost €40 per month at the time of
+the discussion. The maintainer kept SMS: reaching members and avoiding missed pickups and food waste justified
+that cost. Email had already been tried and had performed worse for these members.
+
+These trial results and the decision to keep SMS are recorded in [issue 52](../../notes/issue-52.md).
